{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/129580-thinking-of-dabbling-in-changeling-as-st","id":129580,"title":"Thinking of Dabbling in Changeling as ST","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-09T20:57:52-07:00","id":129580,"title":"Thinking of Dabbling in Changeling as ST","content":"Have played WOD games for many years and absolutely love Changeling. Have never been a ST before, and wondering if anyone has advise for Freeholds. How much detail is needed to run, I am hoping to get a more M\u00f6tley focused game, but both my players end up preferring sandbox. So I am wondering how fleshed out do most ST make the courts, etc before beginning?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2968-corbien","name":"Corbien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T00:48:28-07:00","id":129701,"title":"","content":"My advice:<br /> <br /> 1) Fire out what your players want to play. Not just their Court/Seeming/Kith/Entitlement, but general concept. Get a rough idea of goals. I recommend doing this with all players together with you. Stats are not required yet but if they want to make some general ones thats fine.<br /> <br /> 2) Find out where as a group interests you as a setting. Here, your input is as good as theirs. Pick a location together.<br /> <br /> 3) Ask them about what aspects of the setting they are into. Do they love Oniromancy, or likely never to use it? Do they want a lot of politics, or are they an Ogre bumpkin who tends hedge fruits all day. Figure out what they want. If there is something you want, discuss it with them (&quot;I want to use Hedge realms, do you think your Ogre bumpkin may wander into Hedge realms looking for goblin fruit?&quot;)<br /> <br /> 4) Be sure you know exactly what they expect, and be sure to communicate your own desires. Leave this meeting with everyone, hopefully, having an idea of what they want.<br /> <br /> Example: My game on this forum (feel free to steal shit from it) we decided to play Changeling and literally did a process like this. I suggested I wanted a game set in the Malibu/Santa Monica area; everyone else was fine with it or did not care. Two of them had solid concepts quickly, two had rough concepts quickly, one gave us a list to decide who we liked better. During discussion, running a Burlesque house/Cabaret came up as an idea to unite the Motley, so we decided to do that, and have them meet at the Burlesque house for the first time. By the end of that session, I had a rough idea of 5/6 of the PCs, including Court, Seeming and Kith, and a thumbnail on them. I knew two would want to do some Oniromancy. I knew they would want to run the Cabaret and make it successful. I had two sneaky types, two badasses, and a social dynamo, with no one all that mentally/occult oriented. The 6th made a similar concept. No one had major political ambitions yet but it could change<br /> <br /> From here it is gonna vary.You are going to look at what the needs are in terms of what the group wants. Someone with big political ambitions? Flesh out the power structure of their court, with the idea in mind someone is gonna shake that tree. Hardcore Occultist? Maybe set up some mystic sites or something. Hedge explorer, you are going to need a lot of info on the hedge. I generally recommend allowing, depending on how much time you have, as much as a month to 2.5 months for this. if you have less time, triage; if they like clubbing IC, flesh out the NPCs in the local nightclub scene early, for instance.<br /> <br /> Example: My game had one from each court, plus a Moon and Dawn. I had told the players neither had a real presence in the city and they were cool with that. Everyone was brand new...one literally did not know anyone at all in the city until the PCs entered the house she was squatting in. being so new, for session 1 I came up with each Monarch, one or two other characters per Court, and sent them, essentially, who they had met since arriving. I fleshed people out with an eye for who might come to their Cabaret. Due to a variety of circumstances I did not have a month, so I prepped session one with 8 NPCs, total, in the world and no pictures except for the PCs. Two weeks later session 1 was almost entirely PC interaction, with a handful of other characters met. I then dove in and created about 50 local changelings with pictures (counting the earlier ones) and fleshed out plots based on the PCs.<br /> <br /> Counterexample: When I ran Geist, we literally took 2 months before session 1, maybe 2.5. By the time session 1 hit, I had over 50 NPCs with pictures, ready. typed descriptions of locations, lists of NPCs with pictures they knew handed out, and a strong idea of the entire power structure. It worked great.<br /> <br /> Now, once you have this stuff fleshed out, I recommend you have an event planning early on where you can introduce a number of NPCs. Not immediately, maybe not session 1, but soon enough. Actually I recommend giving them at least one session to slip on their new skins. I used to often try to open with a party or social, and found doing it too fast the player had not quite found the PC's &quot;voice&quot; yet much of the time and so they did not interact as much, or were perhaps unusually animated for the social. You can read your players, are they already arguing about booze IC while stating their PCs, or does one player keep changing their mind about the character's gender even after the meeting? Should give you some idea, but I generally recommend giving a session to slip in, knowing something is coming up to prep for/shop for/hide from/etc.<br /> <br /> Example: In my Changeling game's case, it was the opening of the Cabaret session 3. In Geist case, they had a list of places and were advised that there was often ghostly activity on Walpurgis (24 hours from start time) so they immediately planned how to set up a patrol, which lead to many plot hooks. The old Changeling I ran at a beachfront community I had a huge storm blow in dangerous hobs session 1, and they and many locals worked to fight them off, which got a lot of local NPCs introduced quickly and the Court leaders introduced as they took charge of the situation (or were conspicuously absent)<br /> <br /> That should give a good start. Hope I was not too vague...or specific.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 05-10-2014, 03:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T07:06:16-07:00","id":129871,"title":"","content":"No that's a great example. I know for DND it was easier to DM for me and set up he kingdom in broad strokes. WOD games are just so much more personal and the sandbox seems much bigger haha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2968-corbien","name":"Corbien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}